  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with a spelling change: **z→c before e** to preserve the /s/ (Latin America) or /θ/ (Spain) sound. This affects the yo form of the pretérito indefinido (paralicé, not *paralizé) and every form of the subjuntivo presente and the usted/nosotros/ustedes imperative forms (paralice, paralicemos, paralicen).",
    "No stem change — purely an orthographic adjustment.",
    "Past participle is regular: **paralizado**.",
    "*El accidente paralizó su vida hace veinte años.* (\"The accident brought his life to a standstill twenty years ago.\")",
    "*La huelga paralizó la ciudad por completo.* (\"The strike brought the city to a complete halt.\")",
    "Related: *la parálisis* (paralysis, noun), *paralizado/a* (paralyzed, adjective), other -zar verbs share this pattern (rechazar, abrazar, avanzar, cruzar)."
  ],
